-- title:
--   Level-raising maps between levels N and Nq²: properties
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a local integral domain of characteristic zero, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ which is not a unit in $\mathcal O$, and let $N, q$ be nonzero naturals with $q$ prime and $q \nmid N$. Assume, for each $d \in \{1, q, q^2\}$, the predicate [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) for the pair $(N, Nq^2)$ with full subgroups $H = \top$, $H' = \top$: that is, $N \mid Nq^2$, $d \mid (Nq^2)/N$, and units of $\mathbb Z/Nq^2$ in $H'$ reduce into $H$. Here $H^1(M,\top;\mathcal O)$ is the $\mathcal O$-module $\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M), \mathcal O)$ of additive homomorphisms on $\Gamma_H(M) = \Gamma_0(M)$, `iDegL` is pull-back along the conjugation homomorphism $\Gamma_0(Nq^2) \to \Gamma_0(N)$ attached to $d$, `jDegL` is the transfer (corestriction) back along the image of that homomorphism, and `heckeT`/`heckeTL` are the transfer-composed-with-conjugation Hecke operators $T_\ell$; [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62) is the submodule of homomorphisms satisfying `IsParabolicHom`, i.e. vanishing at every element meeting the parabolicity condition. Put $w = q\,i_1 - i_q \circ T_q + i_{q^2} : H^1(N) \to H^1(Nq^2)$ and $w' = q\,j_{q^2} - T_q \circ j_q + j_1 : H^1(Nq^2) \to H^1(N)$. The conclusion is the conjunction of six assertions: (i) $w$ carries parabolic homomorphisms of level $N$ to parabolic homomorphisms of level $Nq^2$; (ii) $w'$ carries parabolic homomorphisms of level $Nq^2$ to parabolic ones of level $N$; (iii) for parabolic $x, jy$ of level $N$ and $y, wx$ of level $Nq^2$ with $wx = w x$ and $jy = w' y$, the pairings satisfy [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) $\mathcal O\,N\,(jy, x) =$ [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) $\mathcal O\,(Nq^2)\,(y, wx)$; (iv) $w'(w\varphi) = (q-1)\bigl((q+1)^2\varphi - T_q^2 \varphi\bigr)$ for all $\varphi \in H^1(N)$; (v) for every nonzero prime $\ell \neq q$, $w \circ T_\ell = T_\ell \circ w$ on $H^1(N)$; and (vi) for every set $S$ of naturals, every element $b$ of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O} H^1(N,\top;\mathcal O)$ generated by the range of [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) $N\,\top\,S\,\mathcal O$ (the Hecke operators `heckeTL` at the generators of type `Gen` and the diamond operators `diamondL`) preserves parabolic homomorphisms and is self-adjoint for [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) $\mathcal O\,N$, in the form: if $bx$ and $by'$ are parabolic with $bx = b x$ and $by' = b y$, then `Bfam₀` $(bx, y) =$ `Bfam₀` $(x, by')$.
--
--   These are the properties of Wiles's level-raising maps between the cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$ and of $\Gamma_0(Nq^2)$ at a prime $q \nmid N$ — parabolicity, adjointness for the period pairing, the identity $w'w = (q-1)((q+1)^2 - T_q^2)$, and commutation with $T_\ell$ for $\ell \neq q$ — together with preservation and self-adjointness of the whole Hecke algebra at level $N$. They are packaged in exactly the shape needed by the step that carries a Hecke module realised as a local corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(L), \mathcal O)$ through one level-raising step at $q$.
